t leaf duplicated to next power of 2.", "audit_log_algorithm": "SHA-256('merkl-entry-v1' || NUL || workspace_id_16_bytes || session_id_utf8 || session_root_32_bytes || leaf_count_8be || sealed_at_iso_utf8 || sequence_8be || prev_log_hash_32_bytes)", "continuation_algorithm": "For successor sessions: leaf 0 = SHA-256('merkl-binding-v1' || NUL || parent_session_id_utf8 || parent_root_32_bytes || reason_utf8). Proving leaf 0 against successor.root ties the continuation to its parent cryptographically.", "log_tree_algorithm": "RFC 6962 Merkle tree over audit log entry current_hash values in sequence order: leaf = SHA-256(0x00 || entry_hash), node = SHA-256(0x01 || left || right). Inclusion and consistency proofs per RFC 9162 \u00a72.1.", "anchor_algorithm": "The checkpoint body digest is submitted to public OpenTimestamps calendars, which aggregate submissions into Bitcoin transactions. A pending attestation upgrades to a standalone Bitcoin proof once mined; verify with the ots client. Merkl cannot backdate an anchored checkpoint.", "receipt_algorithm": "Receipt leaf = SHA-256('merkl-receipt-leaf-v1' || NUL || leaf_name || NUL || canonical_bytes(content)); an absent leaf hashes the literal null. Seven leaves pad to eight by repeating the last. LEFT = fold(leaves 0-3) is the authorization commitment the policy key signs and the rail's anchor field carries; RIGHT = fold(leaves 4-7); ROOT = SHA-256(LEFT || RIGHT). The envelope's canonical hash is the input_hash of the session action that committed it.", "checkpoint_algorithm": "Ed25519 signature over the checkpoint body bytes (signed-note format: origin, tree_size, base64 root, 'time <unix>' lines, each newline-terminated). Verify with the advertised public key; compare key_id = first 8 bytes of SHA-256(public_key), hex."}}